          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_2218270C_CONCEPTS_01_MOMENT_OF_INERTIA_GYRATION",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR_INERTIA_AND_GYRATION",
          "title": "1. Moment of Inertia and Radius of Gyration",
          "contentMarkdown": "Moment of inertia $I = \\\\sum m_i r_i^2$ measures rotational resistance. It depends on mass, shape, size, and mass distribution relative to the axis. Radius of gyration $k$ is defined by $$I = M k^2$$.",
          "boundAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_2218270C_8CAE2DC0",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_2218270C_21EC7CBE",
